2PdRvWd\\/yY6oAz3eF3pYTViEhBEWO0+ONMMR3DLYU9J4+Z5zQ+nhr5+6zbcM6Ic1DVXYnFxYv\\/13kNf+L\\/TvxHWDPgEjlwsAwV\\/sOoC9VhVdMqVLZVQLSKOCnjZMzKmoUxseMxMnE0Plj9DR694YY\\/Sfsn\\/tf4fwAlchV2QtVjSAAAACV0RVh0ZGF0ZTpjcmVhdGUAMjAyNS0wNy0yNlQwNzowOToyNSswMDowMBv95hIAAAAldEVYdGRhdGU6bW9kaWZ5ADIwMjUtMDctMjZUMDc6MDk6MjUrMDA6MDBqoF6uAAAAKHRFWHRkYXRlOnRpbWVzdGFtcAAyMDI1LTA3LTI2VDA3OjA5OjQxKzAwOjAwD5VS5QAAAABJRU5ErkJggg==\",\"copy_no\":\"001\"}', '{\"show_page_numbers\":true,\"confidentiality_notice\":\"CONFIDENTIAL - For Internal Use Only\",\"footer_text\":\"\"}', '{\"prepared_by\":{\"name\":\"PRASAD (master)\",\"designation\":\"Software Developer\",\"date\":\"2026-02-13\",\"signature\":\"\"},\"reviewed_by\":{\"name\":\"Vivek Patil\",\"designation\":\"Software Developer\",\"date\":\"2026-02-14\",\"signature\":\"\"},\"approved_by\":{\"name\":\"Sagar Sakhare\",\"designation\":\"Software Developer\",\"date\":\"2026-02-18\",\"signature\":\"\"}}', 'master', '142', 'SUBMITTED', '2026-02-13 09:57:10', '2026-02-13 09:57:10');
INSERT INTO `sop_creation_drafts` (`id`, `draft_id`, `template_id`, `template_name`, `header_template_id`, `section_order`, `content`, `section_names`, `document_info`, `header_config`, `footer_config`, `approval_info`, `created_by`, `plant_id`, `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(2, 'DRAFT-1770973110175-7b67jfel6', 'T2', 'Equipment SOP', 'H2', '[\"scope\",\"purpose\",\"abbreviations\",\"roles_responsibilities\",\"procedure\",\"training_requirements\",\"revision_history\"]', '{\"scope\":\"<p>The scope of the raw material sampling Standard Operating Procedure (SOP) is to define the procedures and guidelines for the sampling of raw materials used in pharmaceutical manufacturing. This SOP will outline the responsibilities of personnel involved in the sampling process, the equipment and materials required, as well as the documentation and recording practices to ensure the integrity and traceability of all sampled materials.<\\/p>\",\"purpose\":\"<p>The purpose of the raw material sampling Standard Operating Procedure (SOP) is to establish a systematic process for sampling raw materials used in pharmaceutical manufacturing. This SOP aims to ensure that samples are collected accurately, consistently, and in compliance with regulatory requirements. By following this procedure, we can maintain the integrity of raw materials, prevent contamination, and uphold the quality standards of our final pharmaceutical products.<\\/p>\",\"abbreviations\":\"<p>When writing a Standard Operating Procedure (SOP) for raw material sampling, it is important to use abbreviations to enhance clarity and conciseness. Below are some commonly used abbreviations that can be included in the SOP:<\\/p><ul><li><strong>RMS<\\/strong> - Raw Material Sampling<\\/li><li><strong>SOP<\\/strong> - Standard Operating Procedure<\\/li><li><strong>QA<\\/strong> - Quality Assurance<\\/li><li><strong>QC<\\/strong> - Quality Control<\\/li><li><strong>mg<\\/strong> - milligram<\\/li><li><strong>mL<\\/strong> - milliliter<\\/li><li><strong>%<\\/strong> - percent<\\/li><li><strong>g<\\/strong> - gram<\\/li><li><strong>LIMS<\\/strong> - Laboratory Information Management System<\\/li><\\/ul>\",\"roles_responsibilities\":\"<p>For the Raw Material Sampling SOP, the following roles and responsibilities are defined:<\\/p><ul><li><strong>Quality Control Manager:<\\/strong> Responsible for overseeing the implementation of the sampling procedure and ensuring compliance with SOP.<\\/li><li><strong>Laboratory Technician:<\\/strong> Responsible for carrying out the actual sampling of raw materials as per the defined procedure and documenting the results accurately.<\\/li><li><strong>Warehouse Personnel:<\\/strong> Responsible for providing the necessary raw material samples to the Laboratory Technician and ensuring proper storage and handling of the materials.<\\/li><li><strong>Quality Assurance Officer:<\\/strong> Responsible for conducting periodic audits to ensure that the sampling procedure is being followed correctly and making any necessary updates to the SOP.<\\/li><li><strong>Production Manager:<\\/strong> Responsible for coordinating with the Quality Control Manager to schedule sampling activities in a way that minimally impacts production schedules.<\\/li><\\/ul>\",\"procedure\":\"<p>To ensure the proper sampling of raw materials, follow the procedure outlined below:<\\/p><ol><li>Preparation before Sampling:<ul><li>Ensure all necessary sampling equipment is clean and properly calibrated.<\\/li><li>Review the sampling plan to understand the sampling requirements.<\\/li><li>Verify the identity of the raw material to be sampled.<\\/li><\\/ul><\\/li><li>Sampling Process:<ul><li>Locate the specific area designated for sampling.<\\/li><li>Use appropriate personal protective equipment (PPE) before starting the sampling process.<\\/li><li>Take samples according to the predefined sampling plan and guidelines.<\\/li><li>Record all relevant information such as sample location, date, time, and sampler\'s name.<\\/li><\\/ul><\\/li><li>Post-Sampling Activities:<ul><li>Label the samples with unique identifiers for traceability.<\\/li><li>Transfer the samples to the designated storage area following proper storage conditions.<\\/li><li>Clean and sanitize all sampling equipment used during the process.<\\/li><li>Document any deviations or issues encountered during the sampling process.<\\/li><\\/ul><\\/li><\\/ol>\",\"training_requirements\":\"<p><strong>Training is a critical component of ensuring that all personnel involved in pharmaceutical operations are competent and capable of performing their duties effectively. The following training requirements must be adhered to:<\\/strong><\\/p><ol><li>All personnel must receive initial training upon hire to ensure they are familiar with their roles, responsibilities, and relevant procedures.<\\/li><li>Regular refresher training sessions should be conducted to reinforce knowledge and keep personnel up-to-date on any changes in protocols or regulations.<\\/li><li>Training records must be maintained for each individual, documenting the type of training received, the date it was completed, and the name of the trainer.<\\/li><li>Personnel must demonstrate proficiency in their assigned tasks before being allowed to perform them independently.<\\/li><li>New hires should undergo a period of supervised work to ensure they are adequately trained and competent before working independently.<\\/li><li>Training programs should be periodically reviewed and updated to reflect changes in processes, technologies, or regulations.<\\/li><li>Personnel should be encouraged to participate in additional training opportunities to enhance their skills and knowledge in pharmaceutical operations.<\\/li><\\/ol>\",\"revision_history\":\"<p><strong>Revision History<\\/strong><\\/p><p>Below is the revision history table for the new SOP of raw material sampling:<\\/p><figure class=\\\"table\\\"><table><tbody><tr><th>Version<\\/th><th>Date<\\/th><th>Author<\\/th><th>Description<\\/th><\\/tr><tr><th>1.0<\\/th><th>MM\\/DD\\/YYYY<\\/th><th>[Author\'s Name]<\\/th><th>Initial draft of the SOP<\\/th><\\/tr><tr><th>1.1<\\/th><th>MM\\/DD\\/YYYY<\\/th><th>[Author\'s Name]<\\/th><th>Reviewed and updated sampling procedures<\\/th><\\/tr><tr><th>1.2<\\/th><th>MM\\/DD\\/YYYY<\\/th><th>[Author\'s Name]<\\/th><th>Incorporated feedback from quality assurance<\\/th><\\/tr><tr><th>1.3<\\/th><th>MM\\/DD\\/YYYY<\\/th><th>[Author\'s Name]<\\/th><th>Finalized SOP ready for implementation<\\/th><\\/tr><\\/tbody><\\/table><\\/figure>\"}', '[]', '{\"sop_number\":\"SOP-QA-002\",\"version\":\"1.0\",\"title\":\"Sampling Of Raw Material\",\"effective_date\":\"2026-02-19\"}', '{\"header_template_id\":\"H2\",\"show_main_title\":true,\"show_department\":true,\"show_title\":true,\"show_sop_no\":true,\"show_version_no\":true,\"show_effective_date\":true,\"show_logo\":true,\"company_name\":\"Aurenyx Pharmatech Pvt. Ltd.\",\"show_master_copy\":false,\"show_controlled_copy\":false,\"show_copy_no\":true,\"show_supersede_no\":false,\"show_supersede_version\":false,\"show_next_review_date\":false,\"department\":\"Quality Assurance\",\"logo_path\":\"data:image\\/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAALAAAABCCAYAAAD37VxMAAAAIGNIUk0AAHomAACAhAAA+gAAAIDoAAB1MAAA6mAAADqYAAAXcJy6UTwAAAAGYktHRAD\\/AP8A\\/6C9p5MAAAAHdElNRQfpBxoHCSnmJL6hAAAAAW9yTlQBz6J3mgAAXVRJREFUeNrtvXV4Vcf2P\\/yZ2XY87h4kEAgQ3ClQWmqUulO7bW\\/d9ba37q60pS4UqhQotGhxCJAQSELc\\/ZyT47LPlnn\\/OEkKlSvf732f+\\/7eXz\\/PQ9Mn2Xv27DWfWbNmrTVrE\\/yHEJZlSKKI2rYm9ATb4Nd9g38zUROSpAwU5gxHOBKGQTKAEPKfevSf+L8Y9H96Y0RRwBhDRdtRLNu7DGOXjgcAGiNZbISQTAY2jIENZ2DDAJJtFgyxIKAnfrIQnx38BE29jbj+w6vBGPtvy+BP\\/B+Mf1sNhsNhSJKEspZyfHp4OV4641nDltrNQ+udLeO6Al3jun29hc6wO1XWZCMYCAggUCEcI1rsmTHpVZnWzD35cZml8wsWND2+8Sll0fDTcPHyU1FxXzso\\/R\\/Ppz\\/xfyn+ZQIzxlDeWooRKYVYcWQlLp94uWFF6VczDvdWnt\\/qbT+hN9CX5ZX9RlkNQ9U06GAAGBgAQgBKOZg4CfGmuGCqObEpw5q2cWzy6C\\/PKz7n4MclH0fOH30xyjsOY9rwif9tmfyJ\\/4PwLxFYVVU02usQb4pHgi2ZbK7dVLSvvezy0u4j5zV7OrMiShga0webJNDBQEBBo0QmjBEgSmlGCE8pJF5i+XFZrUVJBZ9PSB37wak3nNrQ9bUH7nAA0MMYmZv\\/35bNn\\/g\\/APw\\/u4Axhjd2voYJGRMwLHWEcUXZinM2Nm6\\/o9rZONYj+6nGGHgQGHhJNwqibBSMPoHyIQCQ1YgY1mRrSAmbFF2ljOmghDCdMYSUMKnsrc\\/p9Hbf0+Rum\\/vZS188nZpkW1\\/bcESt7av8b8vlT\\/wfgn+ogYOhIO5ZdxcWjToT07Km2